<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<exercises xml:id="exercises-3-5">
  <title>Exercises for Section 3.5</title>

  <p>
    These exercises cover the method of undetermined coefficients. For each
    problem, remember: the frequency <m>k</m> in your guess always comes from
    the right-hand side of the ODE, and you should put the ODE in standard form
    (leading coefficient 1) before checking for the case of duplication.
  </p>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Q1: Identification
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <exercise xml:id="ex-3-5-1">
    <title>Identifying the Correct Guess</title>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        For each ODE below, state the correct form of the guess <m>y_p</m>
        for finding a particular solution using undetermined coefficients.
        You do not need to solve for the coefficients.
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-1a">
      <statement>
        <p>
          <m>y'' + 3y' + 2y = 5\cos(4t)</m>
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          Normal case (<m>k = 4</m>, coefficient of <m>y</m> is <m>2 \neq 16 = k^2</m>):
          <me>y_p = A\cos(4t) + B\sin(4t).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-1b">
      <statement>
        <p>
          <m>y'' + 16y = 3\cos(4t)</m>
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          Case of duplication (<m>k = 4</m>, coefficient of <m>y</m> is <m>16 = k^2</m>):
          <me>y_p = t\bigl(A\cos(4t) + B\sin(4t)\bigr).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-1c">
      <statement>
        <p>
          <m>2y'' + 8y = \cos(2t)</m>
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          Dividing through by <m>2</m> gives <m>y'' + 4y = \tfrac{1}{2}\cos(2t)</m>.
          Since <m>k = 2</m> and the coefficient of <m>y</m> is <m>4 = k^2</m>,
          this is the case of duplication:
          <me>y_p = t\bigl(A\cos(2t) + B\sin(2t)\bigr).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-1d">
      <statement>
        <p>
          <m>y'' - 16y = 3\cos(4t)</m>
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          Normal case. Even though <m>k = 4</m> and <m>4^2 = 16</m>, the coefficient
          of <m>y</m> is <m>-16</m>, not <m>+16</m>. The homogeneous equation
          <m>y'' - 16y = 0</m> has real exponential solutions, not trig functions,
          so the usual guess works fine:
          <me>y_p = A\cos(4t) + B\sin(4t).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

  </exercise>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Q2: Three-part question with parameter m
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <exercise xml:id="ex-3-5-2">
    <title>Normal Case vs. Case of Duplication</title>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        Consider the ODE
        <me>my'' + 8y = 8\cos(2t),</me>
        where <m>m</m> is a positive constant.
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-2a">
      <statement>
        <p>
          For what value of <m>m</m> are we in the case of duplication?
        </p>
      </statement>
      <hint>
        <p>
          Divide through by <m>m</m> first to put the ODE in standard form,
          then check whether the coefficient of <m>y</m> equals <m>k^2</m>,
          where <m>k = 2</m> is the frequency on the right-hand side.
          
        </p>
      </hint>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>m = 2.</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-2b">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the general solution for <m>m = 2</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <me>y = c_1\cos(2t) + c_2\sin(2t) + t\sin(2t).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-2c">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the general solution for <m>m = 1</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <me>y = c_1\cos(2\sqrt{2}\,t) + c_2\sin(2\sqrt{2}\,t) + 2\cos(2t).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

  </exercise>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Q3: Normal case with y' term, full IVP
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <exercise xml:id="ex-3-5-3">
    <title>Solving an IVP with a Non-Homogeneous Equation</title>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        Solve the initial value problem
        <me>y'' + 2y' + 5y = 10\cos(t), \quad y(0) = 1, \quad y'(0) = 0.</me>
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-3a">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find the complementary function <m>y_c</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <me>y_c = e^{-t}\bigl(c_1\cos(2t) + c_2\sin(2t)\bigr).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-3b">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find a particular solution <m>y_p</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <me>y_p = 2\cos(t) + \sin(t).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

    <task xml:id="ex-3-5-3c">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Use the initial conditions to find the specific solution to the IVP.
          Remember to apply the initial conditions to the full general solution
          <m>y = y_c + y_p</m>, not just <m>y_c</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <me>y = -e^{-t}(\cos(2t)+\sin(2t)) + 2\cos(t) + \sin(t).</me>
        </p>
      </answer>
    </task>

  </exercise>

  <interactive xml:id="question-form-3-5-ex" iframe="question-form.html?section=3.5 exercises" width="100%" aspect="2:1"/>

</exercises>
